<title>USA: St Paul hogs off $.50 - USDA.</title>
<headline>St Paul hogs off $.50 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>ST PAUL 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Barrows and gilts were $.50</p>
<p>lower in moderate trade. Top $55.00 per cwt. - USDA</p>
<p>US 1-3     220-250 lbs     55.00</p>
<p>	     250-260 lbs     54.50-55.00</p>
<p>	     260-270 lbs     53.50-54.50</p>
<p>US 2-3     270-280 lbs     52.50-53.50</p>
<p>US 2-4     280-290 lbs     51.50-52.50</p>
<p>Sows: under 500 lbs steady; over 500 lbs steady to $1.00</p>
<p>higher. Top 55.00.</p>
<p>US 1-3     300-400 lbs     45.00</p>
<p>	     400-500 lbs     47.00-50.00</p>
<p>	     500-550 lbs     51.00-52.00</p>
<p>	     550-700 lbs     54.00-55.00</p>
</text>
